# Images build from source (apps/*/Dockerfile, context = repo root). Keep local installs, build
# output, secrets and anything the builds don't read out of the context.

# Installs and build output
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts

# Secrets. Dokploy's "Create Environment File" option writes a .env next to the Dockerfile;
# it must never end up in an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local data and test output
**/.storage
**/.dev-mail
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# Repo and editor metadata, docs, and the build files themselves
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.claude
docs
/*.md
docker-compose.yml
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
